  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to repeal section 255.17 of the penal law relating to the crime of\nadultery",
    "basePrintNo": "S8744",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8744-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Rpld §255.17, Pen L",
    "lawSection": "Penal Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8744\n\nSPONSOR: KRUEGER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to repeal section 255.17 of the penal law relating to the crime\nof adultery\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo decriminalize adultery\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 repeals section 255.17 of the penal law.\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis outdated statute criminalizes sexual behavior between consenting\nadults as a Class B Misdemeanor, punishable by up to three months in\nprison and a fine of up to $500. The state has no business regulating\nthe consensual sexual behavior between adults. It is long-past time for\nus to remove this statute from the penal law.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021 - 2022: A100 (Quart)\n\n2019 - 2020:  A11073 (Quart)\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take place immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
